WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Walk down a busy high street and you might

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.070
pass hair salon after hair salon.

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.200
But the water in every home in that town

4
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.500
arrives through one network of pipes,

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.330
run by one company.

6
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.050
And in Britain's grocery market,

7
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.700
just four supermarket groups take
about two thirds of all sales.

8
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.560
Why do some markets have
thousands of sellers while

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.780
others have only one or two?

10
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.960
In this mission, you'll line
up four market structures,

11
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.300
from countless identical
sellers to a single one.

12
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.360
Then you'll use real
supermarket data to measure how

13
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.590
concentrated a market is.

14
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.890
Your mission: find out what
decides how many sellers

15
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.080
a market can hold.
